1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,545
Mechanical design in Blender can have an editable feature history.

2
00:00:04,546 --> 00:00:07,579
This is Blender Parametric CAD.

3
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:14,085
Starting with a simple gear pair, we connect modeling, assembly, and motion in one reproducible workflow.

4
00:00:15,017 --> 00:00:18,654
Start with module, tooth count, and pressure angle.

5
00:00:18,655 --> 00:00:23,374
Here we use module two, twenty teeth, and a twenty-degree pressure angle.

6
00:00:23,375 --> 00:00:28,861
The involute outline becomes ordinary sketch geometry that can be inspected and extruded.

7
00:00:29,767 --> 00:00:36,826
Extrude the profile to create an eight-millimeter face width, then cut a six-point-three-millimeter shaft bore using Through All.

8
00:00:36,827 --> 00:00:41,803
The sketch, extrusion, and bore remain separate features in the model's history.

9
00:00:42,725 --> 00:00:48,352
To change a dimension, edit the upstream extrusion from eight to twelve millimeters, then rebuild.

10
00:00:48,353 --> 00:00:51,374
The through bore follows the updated body.

11
00:00:51,375 --> 00:00:56,326
These images come from the same CAD history evaluated at two different widths.

12
00:00:57,225 --> 00:01:02,342
Link the source parts into an assembly and place them using their pitch-circle center distance.

13
00:01:02,343 --> 00:01:08,107
A twenty-tooth gear driving a forty-tooth gear gives a two-to-one reduction, with opposite rotation.

14
00:01:08,108 --> 00:01:11,494
The animation makes that relationship visible.

15
00:01:12,433 --> 00:01:17,005
Reuse the same parts for compound reductions and planetary gear trains.

16
00:01:17,006 --> 00:01:20,439
Add links and cams to explore other mechanisms.

17
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:27,649
This gallery contains fourteen teaching examples, showing different ways to transmit rotation and produce reciprocating motion.

18
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:36,157
Export each part as a millimeter-scale STL, and keep the dimension, sampled-interference, and save-reopen checks with the project.

19
00:01:36,158 --> 00:01:39,264
Motion here is prescribed by formulas.

20
00:01:39,265 --> 00:01:43,985
Physical print quality and load capacity still require real-world testing.

21
00:01:44,933 --> 00:01:51,216
The repository includes the extension, example models, generation scripts, and animation assets.

22
00:01:51,217 --> 00:01:55,148
Start with your first gear pair, then build your own mechanism.

23
00:01:55,149 --> 00:02:00,974
Explore Blender Parametric CAD on GitHub, and use the Chinese link to switch languages.
